Falsifies `elf::note::verification::note_extent_never_panics`.

The defect: the name's end is added rather than checked. `namesz` is a `u32` from the file and the
cursor can sit anywhere in a segment, so on a 64-bit target this wraps only near `usize::MAX`; the
harness's cursor is unconstrained, which is the point.

Expected to fail: the totality claim, as an arithmetic overflow on `name_start + namesz`.

diff --git a/crates/elf/src/note.rs b/crates/elf/src/note.rs
index 5e21b01e1..161855ab7 100644
--- a/crates/elf/src/note.rs
+++ b/crates/elf/src/note.rs
@@ -203,9 +203,7 @@ fn note_extent(
     if name_start > len {
         return Err(NoteError::Truncated);
     }
-    let name_end = name_start
-        .checked_add(namesz as usize)
-        .ok_or(NoteError::Truncated)?;
+    let name_end = name_start + namesz as usize;
     let desc_start = align_up(name_end, align).ok_or(NoteError::Truncated)?;
     let desc_end = desc_start
         .checked_add(descsz as usize)
